Inspector model artifacts
-------------------------

The public-RIR Reverb encoder/head remain separate CC BY 4.0 artifacts. The
public-effects Drive/Delay branch is integrated as a local non-commercial research
candidate and uses Spotify Pedalboard only as an unbundled GPL-3.0 training
tool. These artifacts are not under the repository's Apache-2.0 license. See:

The bundled temporal Reverb verifier is a local non-commercial research
artifact fitted with private hardware-development recordings plus public
replay. The recordings are not redistributed, and the verifier is not yet
release-qualified because no untouched device-disjoint hardware test exists.

  models/inspector/LICENSES.md
  models/inspector/README.md
  train/LICENSES.md

The rolling non-commercial research Release also embeds
`afx-pedal-identity.onnx`. Its AFx-Rep encoder is Apache-2.0, while its fitted
catalog/verifier heads use ToneTwisT CC BY-NC 4.0 and RemFX `cc-nc` data. The
model is not Apache-2.0 and may not be used for commercial purposes. Full
attribution and the modification notice are in:

  models/inspector/AFX_PEDAL_IDENTITY_NOTICE.md

The routed family-detector weights use the DAFx25 guitar effect-chain corpus, Aachen chapel room
responses, EGFxSet, Guitar-TECHS, and GuitarSet (all CC BY 4.0), plus GuitarJam
(CC0 1.0). IDMT and other restricted research controls are excluded from that
branch; RemFX is used only by the separately licensed identity component.
No source-dataset audio or room response is included in this repository.

